 ### Gradient-based Surface Projection
-Visualizes interfaces between regions of different density by projecting through a matrix of gradient magnitude values [S16]. The surface normal $N$ is approximated by finite differences of neighboring densities, and surface strength $|N|$ is the L2-norm of $N$ [S16]. Surfaces may appear at sub-voxel accuracy due to fractional values, allowing visualization of diffuse transitions [S16].
