 ## Background
 
-The method originates from the need to compute surface normals for shading in volume rendering when analytical derivatives are not available [S12]. It is widely used in interactive volume ray tracing to add visual cues like directional light or Phong shading [S1]. The technique is implemented in various systems, including CGAL's `Finite_difference_gradient_3` for isosurfacing [S12], VolumePro for real-time ray-casting [S9], and GPU Gems for volume rendering techniques [S11]. It is often compared to the Sobel Operator, which provides smoother gradients at the cost of higher computational complexity [S2].
